details.image_prompt:
[
  {
    "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition features two simple, matte ceramic bowls of Lemon-Garlic Chicken and White Bean Soup centered in the frame with generous negative space for a circular crop. Shot from a 3/4 overhead angle at 40 degrees, ensuring every component is clearly identifiable within the broth. Shallow depth of field with one bowl in sharp focus in the foreground and the second bowl softly blurred behind it. Soft natural side lighting coming from a window to the left, casting gentle shadows and creating a subtle, appetizing sheen on the broth's surface. Set on an aged, rustic oak table with visible wood grain and wear. Props include a wooden spoon resting casually against the side of the front bowl and a crumpled linen napkin tucked partially underneath. A single, fresh-looking garlic clove and a few scattered dried Italian herbs sit naturally on the table surface near the bowl. The soup features tender, small crumbles of browned ground chicken, soft mirepoix vegetables, creamy white Great Northern beans, and vibrant, wilted ribbons of baby spinach in a translucent, golden-hued chicken broth. The colors are earthy and warm, with the deep green of the spinach contrasting against the pale white beans and light brown chicken. Small oil droplets float on the surface, catching the natural window light. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating—lived-in, warm, authentic. Slight natural imperfections: a tiny splash of broth on the rim of one bowl, a stray spinach leaf on the table, and uneven ingredient distribution. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from professional editorial food photography for a cookbook."
  }
]
